---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — AI Crossword Maker"
  description="Privacy policy placeholder aligned to actual product behavior. Operator entity required before launch."
  canonicalPath="/privacy/"
>
  <section class="container section prose" style="padding-top:1.5rem;">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p>
      <em>
        Development draft — not counsel-reviewed. Operator legal entity, registered address, and
        privacy contact are <strong>publish blockers</strong>. Do not invent a company name.
      </em>
    </p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Operator entity:</strong> [TO BE FILLED BEFORE LAUNCH]<br />
      <strong>Privacy contact:</strong> [TO BE FILLED — e.g. privacy@your-domain]<br />
      Brand / site: AI Crossword Maker at <code>https://crosswordmaker.app</code>
      (<code>PUBLIC_SITE_URL</code>).
    </p>

    <h2>What we process (product-aligned)</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Local drafts:</strong> stay in your browser IndexedDB until you sign in and save to
        the cloud.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Account:</strong> email (magic link or Google OAuth), optional display name, session
        cookies (HttpOnly).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Cloud puzzles:</strong> titles, grids, clues, versions, activity packs, and share
        tokens you create — stored in Cloudflare D1 / private R2 for exports you request.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Anonymous AI demo:</strong> hashed IP + user-agent for daily quota; optional
        Turnstile token verification. We do not put API keys in the browser.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Billing:</strong> Stripe/Creem process payments. We store order/subscription ledger
        rows and provider customer IDs — not full card numbers.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>AI providers</h2>
    <p>
      When you use AI Topic, prompt content is sent to the configured model provider under their
      terms. Where supported we set <code>store: false</code>. We do not claim zero retention across
      the entire vendor chain.
    </p>

    <h2>Logs &amp; admin</h2>
    <p>
      Operational logs should not store full word lists, clues, or email bodies by default. Admin
      overview shows aggregates and order metadata, not raw puzzle content.
    </p>

    <h2>Before charging customers</h2>
    <p>
      Replace this draft with counsel-reviewed text, fill the operator fields above, and publish a
      working privacy contact. Until then, treat legal pages as incomplete.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
